**What I checked just now:**
- The template's target list contains only this one volume, and its stop condition is still set to "none". Nothing would end an experiment early if it hurt more than intended.
- Both experiments from this template (`EXP7SDntcG3Ff1fsx` and `EXP4Xs8yABzn38YDgv`) are completed.
- The queue-length alarm and the two other `ebs-skill-eval-*` alarms have no notification actions. These experiments change alarm states but don't send any notifications today.

**The plan** passed the safety policy check on the second attempt. The first attempt was rejected because it didn't back up the alarm configuration first; the backup step is now included.

